# Delivery worker configuration (.dev.vars.example)

Copy to `delivery/.dev.vars` for local `wrangler dev`.

```env
# Shared with the API worker/server — tokens minted there are verified here.
JWT_SECRET=your-jwt-secret-at-least-32-chars

# Policy applied to objects that carry NO playback-policy metadata.
# "public" preserves historical behavior; "signed" fails closed.
# Objects transcoded by OpenVOD always carry the metadata, so this only
# matters for hand-written/legacy objects.
DEFAULT_POLICY=public

# Comma-separated user-agent keywords exempt from UA binding
# (native players / casting devices). Default:
# crkey,chromecast,roku,tizen,webos,appletv
CAST_UA_KEYWORDS=crkey,chromecast,roku,tizen,webos,appletv

# Verbose per-request debug logging (raw UA + referer) — off by default.
DELIVERY_DEBUG=false
```

## Required bindings / secrets (wrangler.jsonc)

| Item | How | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `TRANSCODED_BUCKET` R2 binding | `wrangler.jsonc` `r2_buckets` | Point `bucket_name` at your transcoded R2 bucket |
| `USAGE_ANALYTICS` Analytics Engine | `wrangler.jsonc` `analytics_engine_datasets` | Dataset `bandwidth_usage`; write these blobs: org, videoId, fileType; double: bytes |
| `JWT_SECRET` | `wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET` | MUST equal the API-side secret; tokens verify issuer `openvod`, audience `playback` |
| `DEFAULT_POLICY`, `CAST_UA_KEYWORDS`, `DELIVERY_DEBUG` | `wrangler secret put` or vars | Optional overrides |

Deploy with `wrangler deploy` after setting your custom domain route (see the
root README / docs — the repo no longer ships hardcoded routes).
